      "[Signal 2 - aged muscle stem cells epigenetically instruct fibro-adipogenic progenitors: GSE282315 (Mus musculus, score 4, n=9, raw MTX + TSV): the longevity-and-senolytics pick of the day and the first NOVEL MuSC-to-FAP epigenetic-instruction dataset in the archive. The finding inverts the usual fibrosis narrative: the fibrogenic cell is not simply activated by inflammation but is instructed by an aged stem-cell compartment. Aged muscle stem cells directly instruct fibro-adipogenic progenitors to proliferate and adopt a fibrogenic phenotype, and the same phenotype appears in Polycomb Ezh2 loss or in aged mice, with regenerative defects, FAP expansion, fibrosis, and elevated MuSC-secreted interleukin 6 and osteopontin. The molecular layer is the part that matters commercially: in aged MuSCs, H3K27me3 erosion at the NF-kB gene correlates with increased expression and enhanced chromatin recruitment at the IL-6 and Spp1 genes, leading to their activation - so the causal chain is epigenetic erasure at one locus, transcription-factor recruitment at two effector genes, secretion of two ligands, and a downstream FAP expansion phenotype. The pharmacological test is already done in the dataset: blocking IL-6 and osteopontin signalling in co-cultures of aged MuSC and FAPs, or in aged mice, reduced FAP proliferation and muscle fibrosis, and the authors name both ligands as potential pharmacological targets. Why it matters for BB: this is the closest public analogue to the company's anti-fibrotic lane in the skeletal-muscle compartment rather than the lung or liver, and it supplies the specific ingredient BB's fibrosis briefs keep asking for - a stroma-directed intervention where the target sits in the ageing stem-cell niche rather than in the fibroblast itself, with a genetic causality anchor (Ezh2) and a validated blockade. It also connects directly to the senescence programme: the mechanism is age-dependent epigenetic derepression in a stem-cell niche, which is a senescence-adjacent, rather than senescence-per-se, mechanism, so BB should be careful to frame it as ageing-niche instruction rather than as a senolytic result. Two cautions: it is mouse data at n=9 with no human counterpart in the archive, and the archive already carries osteopontin and IL-6 mentions in unrelated contexts - a 2026-10-11 CD84 pro-fibrotic macrophage entry and 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-21 m6A and RBP taxonomy entries - so the differentiation is specifically the niche-to-stroma instruction axis with the Ezh2 anchor, and the brief should be positioned as the muscle-compartment companion to those earlier signals.",
